.TH GLGEARS 1
.SH NAME
glgears \- animate classic OpenGL gears with TinyGL and VirGL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glgears
[
.B -b
.I frames
|
.B -n
.I frames
]
[
.B -o
.I image
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Glgears
runs Brian Paul's three-gear scene in a rio window using
.IR tinygl (2).
.PP
Space pauses rotation, arrow keys rotate the view, and
.B q
quits. Resizing recreates the off-screen color and depth targets.
The window reports frame rate including rendering, readback and presentation.
.PP
.B -n
runs for a fixed number of frames in a window and reports the average rate.
.B -b
runs that many frames without a window at 640 by 480, including pixel
readback but excluding presentation and the initial warm-up frame.
.B -o
runs without a window and saves the final frame in Plan 9 image format.
Without a frame count it renders one measured frame.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/glgears
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR tinygl (2),
.IR gpu (3),
.IR teapot (1)
.SH BUGS
Requires the host owner and a VirtIO GPU with VirGL.
Window frame rates include copies and are limited by the animation timer.
